    "result_text": "All 255 tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe endpoint now returns `capacityWarning: true` when an owner's city already holds **40\u201349 other owners**, while the existing hard 409 rejection at **50** (`RejectOwnerCityAtCapacity`) is untouched.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in `AGENTS.md`:\n\n1. **`AssignOwnerCapacityWarning`** (new function) \u2014 counts the other owners sharing the (normalized: trimmed / whitespace-collapsed / lower-cased) city and sets `capacityWarning = count in [40, 50)`. It never rejects. The normalization matches the rejection rule exactly, so the two thresholds line up.\n\n2. **`Owner`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean capacityWarning` field with accessors, mirroring the existing `bulkSignupWarning` snapshot flag.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted an `assignCapacityWarning` step (governed by `transaction`) after `assignBulkSignupWarning`, before `save`, so the count excludes the owner being created.\n\n4. **`owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`** \u2014 inserted the same step (governed by `readonly-transaction`) between `load` and `respond`, so the flag is recomputed live on read. This is what makes the test's `getOwner(id)` return `true` \u2014 the transient flag isn't persisted, so it must be recomputed rather than relying on a create-time snapshot.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a `capacityWarning` mapping (null-safe, defaulting to `false`), matching the `bulkSignupWarning` pattern.\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` boolean property to the owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nOne design note worth flagging: because the value is recomputed on read (not a persisted create-time snapshot), `capacityWarning` reflects the city's *current* membership \u2014 so an owner created when the city was small can later report `true` once the city fills up. That matches the spec's phrasing (\"when the owner's city already has between 40 and 49 owners\") and is what the GET-based test asserts.",
